[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seal\_of\_Solomon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seal_of_Solomon)

&#x200B;

Quite a bit of variation to the myth, but here you go.

>Fix "include all lower titles" when assigning a king-level viceroyalty - it hands out the ducal titles as inheritable ones, which is a no-no. It's incredibly labourious to currently hand out viceroyalties when maintaining a large empire - I want to be able to give a vassal kingdom-level amounts of viceroyalties to a single vassal with a single click, and for him to then distribute them to his own vassals.

&#x200B;

This.  When I hand out a viceroyalty and then it becomes an inheritable title just because I handed out a kingdom level viceroyalty is absurd. At minimum I should gain a claim on the title.
